("aorta","Aorta",0.3,"The body's largest artery, carrying oxygen-rich blood from the heart.","The aorta is the main highway for blood leaving the heart; all other arteries branch from it.","Its elastic walls stretch with each beat and recoil to keep blood flowing smoothly between beats (Windkessel effect).","Segments: ascending, arch, descending thoracic, abdominal; diameter ≈ 2.5-3.5 cm; pulse wave velocity ≈ 4-10 m/s rises with stiffness.",[("Diameter","≈ 2.5-3 cm"),("Length","≈ 40 cm")],"The aorta's elastic recoil keeps blood moving between heartbeats.","aorta",[CV],["smooth_muscle_tissue","dense_connective_tissue","epithelial_tissue"]),
