("artery","Artery",0.004,"Thick-walled vessels carrying blood away from the heart.","Arteries are strong tubes with muscular walls that handle high pressure.","They branch into smaller arterioles.","Three layers (intima, media, adventitia); elastic arteries (aorta) and muscular arteries; arterioles are the main site of resistance.",[("Diameter","≈ 0.1-30 mm"),("Mean pressure","≈ 90-100 mmHg")],"Arteries are named for the Greek for 'air pipes' since they were found empty after death.",None,[CV],["smooth_muscle_tissue","dense_connective_tissue","epithelial_tissue"]),
("vein","Vein",0.005,"Thin-walled vessels returning blood to the heart.","Veins are wider and softer than arteries and have valves to stop blood falling backward.","Squeezing leg muscles pushes blood up through them.","Hold ≈ 60-70% of blood volume (capacitance vessels); valves prevent backflow; varicose veins arise from valve failure.",[("Share of blood volume","≈ 60-70%"),("Pressure","≈ 5-10 mmHg")],"Your veins hold most of your blood at any moment.",None,[CV],["smooth_muscle_tissue","dense_connective_tissue","epithelial_tissue"]),
