O("nose_airway","Nose, nasal cavity and pharynx","structure",0.12,"The upper airway that warms, moistens and filters air.","Air enters through the nose, where hairs and mucus trap dust, and warms up on its way to the lungs.","The nasal cavity has a rich blood supply and mucus-coated lining with cilia.","Turbinates create turbulent flow to humidify air to ≈ 100% relative humidity at body temperature; olfactory epithelium sits at the roof.",[("Air warming","to ≈ 37 C"),("Humidification","≈ 100%")],"Your nose alternates which nostril is dominant every few hours.",[RS],["epithelial_tissue","smooth_muscle_tissue"],["breathing"],sec="22.1",kn=("respiratory_physiology",))
O("larynx","Larynx","organ",0.05,"The voice box that guards the airway and produces sound.","The larynx holds your vocal cords. They vibrate when air passes to make your voice.","Cartilages and muscles move the vocal folds, and the epiglottis closes the airway when you swallow.","Phonation by Bernoulli effects and mucosal wave; fundamental frequency ≈ 100-120 Hz (typically lower voices) to ≈ 200-250 Hz; superior and recurrent laryngeal nerves.",[("Vocal fold length","≈ 1.2-2.5 cm"),("Voice pitch (typical)","≈ 85-255 Hz")],"Your voice pitch is set by vocal-fold length and tension, not by 'size of the throat'.",[RS],["epithelial_tissue","cartilage_tissue"],["breathing"],mesh="larynx",sec="22.1",kn=("respiratory_physiology",))
O("trachea","Trachea (windpipe)","organ",0.11,"A flexible tube reinforced by C-shaped cartilage rings that carries air to the lungs.","The windpipe leads from the throat to the lungs and is kept open by rings of cartilage.","Its inner lining of ciliated cells sweeps mucus and trapped dust upward (mucociliary escalator).","16-20 C-shaped hyaline cartilage rings; posterior trachealis muscle permits esophageal expansion; bifurcates at the carina near T4-T5.",[("Length","≈ 10-12 cm"),("Diameter","≈ 2 cm")],"Cilia in your airways beat about 10-15 times each second.",[RS],["epithelial_tissue","cartilage_tissue"],["breathing"],mesh="trachea",sec="22.1",kn=("respiratory_physiology",))
